{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f1e153dd3a9e4b81","name":"Weapon Groups","source":{"id":"source:reference-f1e153dd3a9e4b81","title":"Weapon Groups","revision":18608,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:24:36Z","sha256":"539ec6eb26c4fe47f9a41acb09cf5d5bb929535bac042e445234d9e02468702e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18608","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Weapon%20Groups&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f1e153dd3a9e4b81","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Discriminating combatants choose their weapons very carefully. However, a character who knows how to load and fire a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Slugthrower Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Slugthrower_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:e459022b556f2193"}," can handle a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," just as expertly. Thus, weapons are categorized based on their form and function, and a character who takes the appropriate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency"}," feat is considered skilled with all of the weapons in that group. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons"}," such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bowcasters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bowcasters"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flamethrowers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flamethrowers"}," are exceptions: an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," is unique in form and function, and requires special training (that is, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon Proficiency"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon_Proficiency","referenceId":"reference:a5501acefbb91ccb"}," feat) to wield proficiently.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If you are proficient with at least one weapon in a Weapon Group, you qualify to take ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Focus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Focus","referenceId":"reference:393613c18e211d0f"}," (or any other weapon-specific ability) for that Weapon Group. The benefits of such abilities apply only to weapons in which you are Proficient. For example, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," with the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Spacehound"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spacehound"}]}," Talent is proficient with all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Weapons"}," (all of which are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"},"), so they qualify to take ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Focus (Heavy Weapons)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Focus_(Heavy_Weapons)"},". This grants them a +1 bonus on attack rolls with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Weapons"},", but they wouldn't get that benefit with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grenade Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grenade_Launcher","referenceId":"reference:da6a8268b875d982"},", or any other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapon"},", until becoming proficient with them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Weapon Groups"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following are the 7 different Weapon Groups in the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars Roleplaying Game"]},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Advanced Melee Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Advanced_Melee_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:ffc93dd82af566f8"},":"]}," Technologically enhanced melee weapons, primarily using vibration technology."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"},":"]}," Large ranged weapons that require both hands, and in some cases a tripod, to accurately use."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},":"]}," Swords of pure energy, typically used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Traditions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Traditions","referenceId":"reference:da4e2621bc8ff060"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Pistols"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pistols","referenceId":"reference:e660061b7b03b794"},":"]}," Hand-held ranged weapons, favored for self-defense, and are easily concealed."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rifles","referenceId":"reference:a6ebe3ecc8b0b281"},":"]}," Standard military weapons, used with both hands for precise and accurate shooting."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Simple Weapons:"]}," Basic weapons, both melee and ranged, that are simple or primitive in nature and use. Also included are handheld explosives.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Grenades"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grenades","referenceId":"reference:0288f85b407ca487"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapons (Melee)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapons_(Melee)","referenceId":"reference:cd7a4aafaae07eb3"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapons (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapons_(Ranged)","referenceId":"reference:8456b42e685346fd"}]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Exotic Weapons:"]}," Unusual, or unique weapons, both melee and ranged, that require specific training to properly utilize.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons (Melee)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons_(Melee)","referenceId":"reference:e0213365f7fdde76"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons_(Ranged)","referenceId":"reference:c954289d43de9110"}]}]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Improvised Weapons"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Sometimes objects not crafted to be weapons can be used: chairs, bottles, crates, and so on. Because these objects are not designed for such use, characters who use Improvised Weapons are treated as not proficient with them and take a -5 penalty on their attack rolls. The GM determines the size and damage dealt by an Improvised Weapon.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sometimes such Improvised Weapons can be ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thrown"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thrown"}," in a dangerous manner: small rocks, vases, pitchers, and so forth. Because these objects are not designed for such use, characters who use Improvised Thrown Weapons are treated as not proficient with them and take a -5 penalty on their attack rolls.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
